  "id": "untitled",
  "title": "Tiki-Taka Gate Rotation",
  "description": "Pass into the middle, combine through three cone gates, dribble to the far line, then repeat back on the mirrored side.",
  "tags": ["passing", "combination-play", "one-touch", "rotation"],
  "notes": "Keep the middle player available on an open body shape. The runner follows each return pass to the next gate. Use firm, accurate passes through the gates and play one touch when the weight is right. At the end cone, the receiver keeps the ball and joins the far line. The pattern then comes back along the upper side so both feet and both passing angles are trained.",
